Two concurrently launched, individually filtered proof processes did not
initially provide usable evidence.  They were diagnostics, not the submitted
positive command, and the affected claim was rerun successfully.

$ export PATH="$HOME/.nix-profile/bin:$PATH"; kprove spec.k --definition proof-kompiled --spec-module SPEC -I . --claims SPEC.example-nested
Error: K requires Java 17 to run but the detected version is .
Please either add Java 17 bin directory to the PATH or set the JAVA_HOME
environment variable accordingly.
exit=2

Sequential rerun: #Top, exit=0 (recorded in 03_positive_claims.log).

$ export PATH="$HOME/.nix-profile/bin:$PATH"; kprove spec.k --definition proof-kompiled --spec-module SPEC -I . --claims SPEC.main --trusted SPEC.loop
[no output for more than 12 minutes; manually interrupted]
exit=130

Filtering out SPEC.loop before trying to mark it trusted removes the reusable
claim from the selected spec.  Keeping both labels selected closes immediately:

$ export PATH="$HOME/.nix-profile/bin:$PATH"; kprove spec.k --definition proof-kompiled --spec-module SPEC -I . --claims SPEC.main,SPEC.loop --trusted SPEC.loop
#Top
exit=0
